  "updated": "2026-10-27",
  "description": "Curated worked-example repositories. This file is the trust root, on the same terms as widgets/packs.json: an example is admitted only at a full commit SHA, only from a curated owner, and every file it may fetch is pinned by digest here. A branch is never fetched, because a digest pinned against a moving ref verifies nothing.\n\nAn example is a RESOURCE -- a workflow document, data and a provenance record -- and declares no node type, so runtimeFetching: \"none\" in widgets/packs.json does not reach it. That rule governs widget definitions. See docs/experiments/127-examples-as-repositories.md.",
  "governance": {
    "curatedOwners": [
      "digital-twin-ph"
    ],
    "fetchPolicy": "Only on an explicit practitioner action, never on load. Opening an example tells a server it was opened, which is the same disclosure the basemaps and Overpass make, and it is named in the interface and recorded in the receipt.",
    "verification": "Every fetched file is digested with SubtleCrypto and compared to this catalog. A mismatch is a refusal, not a warning.",
    "offline": "An example opened once is cached and stays available. Until it is opened it is FETCHABLE rather than AVAILABLE, and the interface must say which."
  },
  "examples": [
