      "usesNote": "The node types the pinned bundle's workflows instantiate, DECLARED HERE rather than read from the clone, so widgets/evidence.json is the same on a machine that has the checkout and one that does not. A generated ledger whose value depends on what somebody happens to have cloned is not a measurement. validate:examples recomputes this list from the bundle wherever the checkout exists and refuses on a difference, so the declaration cannot drift from the bytes it describes.",
      "largePlateNote": "geo/map2-large.jpg is in the example repository at 5,341,773 bytes and is deliberately NOT pinned here. It is the same plate as geo/map2.jpg, sharing one georeference, and pinning it would multiply what a reader fetches by about fourteen for detail a figure at screen size cannot show. The small plate is about 16 metres per pixel over south London, which is ground. Anyone wanting the 5000-pixel scan has the repository and its digest."
